                "type": "text",
                "text": "Subtract triples containing consecutive integers, correcting for triples counted twice.",
                "marks": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ]
      },
      "worked": "There are $\\binom{20}{3}=1140$ equally likely selections.\n\nFor a selection containing consecutive integers, choose one of the 19 consecutive pairs and then one of the 18 remaining integers. Each of the 18 triples of three consecutive integers is counted twice, so subtract these once.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}N(\\text{at least one consecutive pair})&=19\\times18-18\\\\N(\\text{at least one consecutive pair})&=324\\\\\\Pr(\\text{no two consecutive})&=\\frac{1140-324}{1140}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{no two consecutive})&=\\frac{816}{1140}\\\\\\Pr(\\text{no two consecutive})&=\\frac{68}{95}.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 65
